        <h2>
          Final thoughts
        </h2>


        <p>

          Choosing the right home tutor is ultimately about finding a
          suitable match between the tutor and the student's needs.

        </p>


        <p>

          Start by identifying what your child needs help with. Then
          compare tutors based on relevant subject knowledge, teaching
          experience, communication, teaching approach, availability
          and how they plan to monitor progress.

        </p>


        <p>

          Most importantly, avoid choosing a tutor solely because of
          promises of higher marks. A good tutoring arrangement should
          focus on helping the student understand concepts, practise
          effectively and gradually become more independent in their
          learning.

        </p>



